// Two totals of the distance price travelled against the other side of the
// previous bar, each divided by the total true range over the same window.
//
// Exercises: two warmups that differ by one bar in the same study, because both
// movement terms reach across a bar boundary and the range they are divided by
// does not.

version 1

study("Vortex", precision = 4)

len = input(14, "Length", min = 2, max = 500)

// Both terms are absent on bar 0, and so is any total over a window holding it.
// The true range is not: the bar's own range is a true statement about that bar
// even with no bar before it, which is why the denominator is ready one bar
// earlier than the two numerators.
upMove   = abs(high - low[1])
downMove = abs(low - high[1])

rangeTotal = sum(trueRange(), len)

plot(sum(upMove, len) / rangeTotal, "Upward", aqua, width = 2)
plot(sum(downMove, len) / rangeTotal, "Downward", red, width = 2)
